# AMD64 thunk export spec -- dxva2.dll.
#
# From the 2026-08-17 corpus pass.  Boltgun imports this module STATICALLY and
# it had no guest thunk, so the loader refused the native ppc64 module
# (c000007b) and the whole image failed to load (c0000135).  Measured: the
# exe's import table names DXVA2CreateDirect3DDeviceManager9 (ordinal 1) and
# nothing else -- UE4's hardware video-decode probe.
DLL dxva2.dll
FROM-SPEC auto

# dxva2api.h is not in the oracle's default translation unit, and it does not
# compile on its own: it names D3DFORMAT and D3DPOOL, which come from
# d3d9types.h.  So d3d9.h is appended FIRST and dxva2api.h second -- order
# matters, PROBE-EXTRA lines are emitted in the order written.  Without them
# every export was refused as "no declaration found in Wine headers".
#
# 35 of the 37 exports remain refused for that same reason: the DXVA2 surface
# is declared almost entirely in the .idl's interfaces rather than as flat
# prototypes, and this generator describes flat exports.  The one Boltgun
# actually names is not among them -- DXVA2CreateDirect3DDeviceManager9 is
# declared at dxva2api.h:1555 and is emitted.  Each of the other 35 keeps its
# ordinal as a named sentinel, so a guest that calls one faults BY NAME.
PROBE-EXTRA   d3d9.h
PROBE-EXTRA   dxva2api.h
